# Copy this file to .env.local and fill in real values.
# The two NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_* values are read for real now, by
# src/lib/db/client.ts — `npm run dev` and `npm run test:e2e` fail without them.
# The rest are still placeholders for features that do not exist yet.
# The RLS test suite does not use this file; it reads the local stack's URL and keys
# straight from `supabase status`, so there is nothing to keep in sync by hand.

# Supabase (Postgres + PostGIS, Auth, Realtime, Storage)
# For local development, get real values from `supabase status`.
# Do NOT put actual values (even local-only ones) here — this file is committed
# and must remain a template for new developers.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=
# Server-only — never expose this to the browser (AGENTS.md §8). It bypasses RLS.
# Source: `supabase status`
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=

# Google Maps JavaScript API
# Read by the hero map (src/components/DanceMap.tsx). Without it the map area
# says so in Hebrew and the dance list below still works — the map is an
# enhancement, not a precondition.
NEXT_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_MAPS_API_KEY=
# Advanced markers refuse to render without a map id — Google's requirement, not
# ours, and they are what makes a pin focusable for a keyboard user. Left empty
# the app falls back to Google's public DEMO_MAP_ID, which works but cannot
# carry cloud-side styling; a real project-owned id belongs here before launch.
NEXT_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_MAPS_MAP_ID=

# Cloudflare Turnstile
# The CAPTCHA on the phone-OTP request path (docs/decisions/0013). Every press of
# "שליחת קוד" asks Supabase to spend money on an SMS, so /auth/v1/otp is challenged;
# GoTrue enforces it server-side, and this is only the site key the widget renders
# with. Public by nature — it ships in the HTML — but still not committed here, per
# the rule at the top of this file.
#
# LOCAL: use Cloudflare's published always-passes test site key,
#   1x00000000000000000000AA
# which pairs with the test secret already in supabase/config.toml. No Cloudflare
# account needed to run the app or the tests.
#
# DEPLOYED: a real site key from the Cloudflare Turnstile dashboard, and its matching
# secret set in the Supabase dashboard (Authentication → Attack Protection). The test
# pair must never reach a deployed project — it verifies every token, which would
# disable the control entirely on the one endpoint that costs money.
#
# Left empty, /profile says sign-in is unavailable rather than rendering a form whose
# button can only ever fail.
NEXT_PUBLIC_TURNSTILE_SITE_KEY=

# Web Push (VAPID)
VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY=
VAPID_PRIVATE_KEY=

# Demo mode
# Set to "true" (nothing else) to show the "הסתר הרקדות" toggle in AppHeader —
# a display-only switch that hides every dance from the map and the schedule
# on tap, for showing the app with an empty state. Never set this in a
# production environment: AppHeader and the schedule page read it server-side,
# and left unset (the default) the toggle button is never rendered on either
# screen, so a real dancer gets no control and no way to trigger it.
NEXT_PUBLIC_DEMO_MODE=

# Demo login (Phase 4.2, docs/decisions/0018)
# Set to "true" (nothing else) to replace the real phone-OTP form on /profile with
# the demo sign-in: type a number, press אישור, land on a SEEDED account. 0 is the
# מרקיד; 1 and up are רוקדים.
#
# NEVER set this in production. Note it is deliberately NOT NEXT_PUBLIC_* — it must
# stay server-side, because the credential-issuing Server Action checks this exact
# variable before it will issue anything. Hiding the form is not the gate; that
# check is. A build with this unset has no demo sign-in path at all, which
# tests/rls/roleAndDemoLogin.test.ts asserts by looking for the absence of a
# session rather than the absence of a button.
#
# Even set, it only reaches the four accounts in src/lib/auth/demoUsers.ts, which
# exist only in supabase/seed.sql (local stack) and whose phones are only test
# numbers under [auth.sms.test_otp] in supabase/config.toml (local config). All
# four of those have to line up, which is why this cannot work against a hosted
# project even by accident.
DEMO_LOGIN_ENABLED=
